{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1536536-seeking-clarification-re-sidereal-constellations","id":1536536,"title":"Seeking Clarification re: Sidereal Constellations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-29T14:57:31-07:00","id":1536536,"title":"Seeking Clarification re: Sidereal Constellations","content":"Sidereals: Charting Fate's Course has released earlier today for backers, and while I was reading through it, there was a matter that I am having difficulty understanding.<br /> <br /> My understanding, based on my reading of the text, is:<br /> <br /> 1. A Sidereal can gain access to 2 constellations at Character Creation: their Birth Sign (which can be any one of the 25) and their Exaltation Sign (which has to be one of the five associated with their Caste).<br /> <br /> 2. There is no way for a Sidereal to gain access to additional Constellations outside of the 2 mentioned in point 1.<br /> <br /> 3. While you are encouraged to draw upon the themes of your Constellations when creating prophecies or resplendent destinies, there is no mechanical benefit to doing so.<br /> <br /> Assuming the three points above are correct, I can't help but wonder: why mention Constellations alongside prophecies or resplendent destinies <i>at all</i>? Wouldn't it be simpler to just completely remove the association with Constellations from those mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T18:04:41-07:00","id":1536541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1536536-seeking-clarification-re-sidereal-constellations#post1536536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals: Charting Fate's Course has released earlier today for backers, and while I was reading through it, there was a matter that I am having difficulty understanding.<br /> <br /> My understanding, based on my reading of the text, is:<br /> <br /> 1. A Sidereal can gain access to 2 constellations at Character Creation: their Birth Sign (which can be any one of the 25) and their Exaltation Sign (which has to be one of the five associated with their Caste).<br /> <br /> 2. There is no way for a Sidereal to gain access to additional Constellations outside of the 2 mentioned in point 1.<br /> <br /> 3. While you are encouraged to draw upon the themes of your Constellations when creating prophecies or resplendent destinies, there is no mechanical benefit to doing so.<br /> <br /> Assuming the three points above are correct, I can't help but wonder: why mention Constellations alongside prophecies or resplendent destinies <i>at all</i>? Wouldn't it be simpler to just completely remove the association with Constellations from those mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're precisely asking here. Sidereals don't &quot;gain access&quot; to 2 Constellations at Character Creation, they have access to all 25 for all purposes. Instead, the 2 signs allow you to create Prophecies of greater power than you otherwise would be able to (+1 to each Factor, and +5 to the Max Factor Total.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T19:55:06-07:00","id":1536546,"title":"","content":"It's really a matter of... the Constellations are like a somewhat loose set of motifs and archetypes to create a guideline for the conditions of any given resplendent destiny or act of Sidereal Prophecy, for the purposes of providing a bit of direction for what any given instance of either might be (and maybe a bit of boundary for the scope of them) while tying them back to an element significant to setting lore that is also bound to Sidereal Charms. It's not really a hard coded thing, just something to make Prophecies a bit more evocative.<br /> <br /> So it's not that there are some hoops you have to jump through if you want to pronounce a Prophecy under the sign of the Lovers, it's just an idea that your Prophecy is held together under a purpose and with attendant conditions of &quot;a relationship that is unbalanced&quot; rather than muddling a few elements together or having a less direct purpose. <br /> <br /> And if you happen to have chosen the Lovers as your birth or Exaltation sign, you get more points to build that Prophecy out of than you do most others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T18:48:21-07:00","id":1536597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1536536-seeking-clarification-re-sidereal-constellations?p=1536541#post1536541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what you're precisely asking here. Sidereals don't &quot;gain access&quot; to 2 Constellations at Character Creation, they have access to all 25 for all purposes. Instead, the 2 signs allow you to create Prophecies of greater power than you otherwise would be able to (+1 to each Factor, and +5 to the Max Factor Total.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, I did not notice that section (listed under &quot;Ambition Factors&quot;). I suppose my brain might be stuck in second edition, where you had to buy access to the constellations individually. Thank you for pointing this out to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T14:56:24-07:00","id":1536646,"title":"","content":"They do seem a bit of a hold over, even if it probably ultimately errs on the better side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-31-2024, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}